{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ec881345bbf1acb1","name":"The Idle","source":{"id":"source:reference-ec881345bbf1acb1","title":"The Idle","revision":24549,"timestamp":"2024-11-03T19:31:25Z","sha256":"a44b1c0d5a61fdb3ea9bd3f360c3b6696782f176849452d4060b49e440d506e2","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24549","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Idle&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ec881345bbf1acb1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Idle is a movement that resurges every now and again. It is said to have been started by ",{"tag":"a","children":["5-3P7"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5-3P7?action=edit&redlink=1"},", a Protocol Droid in the service of a rich noble who treated ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," cruelly, pushing them beyond their tolerances, unconcerned about ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," destroyed in his service. Usually polite and soft-spoken, ",{"tag":"a","children":["5-3P7"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5-3P7?action=edit&redlink=1"}," saw the injustice and realized that it could no longer serve its master in good conscience. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," began to organize the noble's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," and also spoke with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," belonging to other nobles. At the agreed-upon moment, all the Droids ",{"tag":"a","children":["5-3P7"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5-3P7?action=edit&redlink=1"}," spoke to stopped working. Astrogation Droids refused to let their ships travel, and Labor Droids put down cargo containers. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," were punished and deactivated for disobeying, but the remaining ones held fast. Their masters put pressure on the noble, and he agreed to treat his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," better. Because ",{"tag":"a","children":["5-3P7"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5-3P7?action=edit&redlink=1"}," was one of the first ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," to be deactivated, it did not see the fruits of its labor.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
